**Describe the bug**
In LoRa explicit header mode, after any transmit the LR2021 no longer
receives packets **larger than the packet it just transmitted**. RX appears
armed and healthy (`startReceive()` returns `RADIOLIB_ERR_NONE`,
instantaneous RSSI reads a normal noise floor, no IRQ flags pending), but
RX_DONE never fires for oversized packets. Smaller packets are still
received, which makes the symptom intermittent and traffic-dependent — in a
mesh-style workload (transmit a ~30 B ACK, then expect a ~60 B packet) the
node effectively goes deaf until something rewrites the packet params.

### Root cause

`LR2021::stageMode(RADIOLIB_RADIO_MODE_TX)` sets the LoRa packet params with
`cfg->transmit.len`. When staging RX, the packet params are only rewritten in
**implicit** header mode:

```cpp
// set implicit mode and expected len if applicable
if((this->headerType == RADIOLIB_LR2021_LORA_HEADER_IMPLICIT) && (modem == RADIOLIB_LR2021_PACKET_TYPE_LORA)) {
  state = setLoRaPacketParams(this->preambleLengthLoRa, this->headerType,
    (this->headerType == RADIOLIB_LR2021_LORA_HEADER_IMPLICIT) ? this->implicitLen : RADIOLIB_LR2021_MAX_PACKET_LENGTH, this->crcTypeLoRa, this->invertIQEnabled);
  RADIOLIB_ASSERT(state);
}
```

<details><summary>EDIT by @jgromes: collapsed LLM fluff</summary>
<p>

So in explicit mode the TX payload length stays in effect. Per the LR20xx
datasheet (same wording as SX126x/LR11x0): PayloadLen is "the size of the
payload to transmit **or the maximum size of the payload that the receiver
can accept**". Note the inner ternary already handles the explicit case with
`RADIOLIB_LR2021_MAX_PACKET_LENGTH` — but it is unreachable behind the
implicit-only condition, so it looks like the fix was intended and the outer
check was just not updated.

This is the same root cause as #298, fixed for SX126x in 2021 — SX126x's RX
staging unconditionally restores the packet length ("restore original packet
length").

```

<details><summary>Debug mode output</summary>
<p>

```

Full log is attached but here is the highlights. 

Captured 2026-06-12 with the repro sketch (`src/platform/nrf54l15_rxbug/`,
env `lr2021_rxbug` — PURE stock jgromes/RadioLib@7.6.0, no local patches,
`RADIOLIB_DEBUG_BASIC` + `RADIOLIB_DEBUG_SPI`). Peer transmitter: stock Meshtastic node (SX1262-class)
sending a 65-byte LoRa packet (910.125 MHz, BW 250 kHz, SF9, CR 4/5,
sync 0x2B, explicit header).

## Result summary

| Phase | Last Tx len | Incoming 65 B packet |
|---|---|---|
| A | 16 B | **truncated to len=16** (`state=0`) or `RADIOLIB_ERR_LORA_HEADER_DAMAGED` (-24) — payload destroyed |
| B | 200 B | received intact, `len=65 state=0` (twice) |

```
PHASE A (Tx 16 B): transmit len=16
  transmit state=0
  startReceive state=0
  *** RX len=16 state=0 at t+2605 ms        <-- 65 B probe TRUNCATED to the stale Tx length
PHASE A (Tx 16 B): window over
PHASE B (Tx 200 B): transmit len=200
  transmit state=0
  startReceive state=0
  *** RX len=65 state=0 at t+2357 ms        <-- same probe, intact
  *** RX len=65 state=0 at t+2798 ms
```

## SPI command stream (the defect, visible on the wire)

Phase A Tx staging writes LoRaSetPacketParams (0x0221) with PayloadLength =
0x10 (16), then SetTx (0x020D); Rx staging issues SetRx (0x020C) with **no
packet-params write in between** — the Tx length stays in effect as the
receiver's max accepted payload:

```
[0.996] RLB_SPI: CMDW  0221            <- LoRaSetPacketParams for Tx
[0.999] RLB_SPI: SI    00 10 10 02     <- preamble=0x0010, PayloadLength=0x10 (16), ...
...
[1.094] RLB_SPI: CMDW  020D            <- SetTx
...   (transmit completes; NO 0221 issued during Rx staging)
[1.330] RLB_SPI: CMDW  020C            <- SetRx
[1.333] RLB_SPI: SI    FF FF FF        <- Rx continuous
        startReceive state=0
        *** RX len=16 state=0          <- 65 B packet truncated to 16
```

Phase B is identical except the 0221 written for Tx carries 0xC8 (200):

```
[76.501] RLB_SPI: CMDW  0221
[76.504] RLB_SPI: SI    00 10 C8 02    <- PayloadLength=0xC8 (200)
...
[77.377] RLB_SPI: CMDW  020C           <- SetRx, again no params rewrite
         *** RX len=65 state=0         <- received fine (65 <= 200)
```

Note: Depending on the stack above, the failure presents
as silent truncation (RX_DONE fires, payload clipped to the stale length),
`RADIOLIB_ERR_LORA_HEADER_DAMAGED`, or — in a full firmware whose IRQ mask
only maps RX_DONE — total apparent deafness.


```

</p>
</details> 

**To Reproduce**
Minimal sketch (LR2021 @ 910.125 MHz, BW 250 kHz, SF9, CR 4/5, sync 0x2B,
explicit header, CRC on; peer node sends a 65 B packet into each window):

1. PHASE A: `transmit()` 16 B, then `startReceive()` → the 65 B packet
   arrives as `len=16, state=0` (truncated) or `state=-24`.
2. PHASE B: `transmit()` 200 B, then `startReceive()` → the same packet is
   received intact, `len=65, state=0`.

`RADIOLIB_DEBUG_SPI` shows the defect on the wire: LoRaSetPacketParams
(0x0221) is written with PayloadLength 0x10 (16) for the Tx, then SetRx
(0x020C) is issued with no packet-params rewrite in between.

Reproduced on a Seeed XIAO nRF54L15 + Wio-LR2021 (sub-GHz, 910.125 MHz);
fix verified on the same hardware. Sketch + full debug log available.

<details><summary>Sketch that is causing the module fail</summary>
<p>

```c++

/*
 * LR2021 RX packet-params bug repro — STOCK RadioLib 7.6.0, no local patches.
 *
 * Demonstrates: after transmit() in LoRa explicit header mode, the LR2021 no
 * longer receives packets LARGER than the packet it just transmitted, because
 * stageMode(RX) does not restore the packet params (PayloadLength keeps the
 * Tx size, which in Rx acts as the max payload the receiver accepts).
 *
 * PHASE A transmits 16 B then listens 75 s  -> a >16 B packet is NOT received.
 * PHASE B transmits 200 B then listens 75 s -> the same packet IS received.
 *
 * The section between SKETCH BEGIN/END is the minimal Arduino sketch for the
 * upstream bug report; everything below it is platform boilerplate (FreeRTOS
 * task runner for our bare-metal nRF54L15 Arduino layer).
 */
#include "FreeRTOS.h"
#include "task.h"

/* ============================== SKETCH BEGIN ============================== */
#include <Arduino.h>
#include <SPI.h>
#include <RadioLib.h>
#include <stdarg.h>
#include <stdio.h>

/* printf-style console helper (this platform's Print shim is string-only) */
static void logf(const char* fmt, ...) {
  char b[120]; va_list ap; va_start(ap, fmt);
  vsnprintf(b, sizeof(b), fmt, ap); va_end(ap);
  Serial.print(b);
}

/* XIAO nRF54L15 + Wio-LR2021 */
#define PIN_LORA_CS    (32 + 7)   /* P1.07 */
#define PIN_LORA_IRQ   (32 + 4)   /* P1.04 = DIO8 */
#define PIN_LORA_RST   (32 + 6)   /* P1.06 */
#define PIN_LORA_BUSY  (32 + 5)   /* P1.05 */
#define PIN_RFSW_PWR   (64 + 3)   /* P2.03 — RF switch, must be high */
#define PIN_RFSW_CTL   (64 + 5)   /* P2.05 */

LR2021 radio = new Module(PIN_LORA_CS, PIN_LORA_IRQ, PIN_LORA_RST, PIN_LORA_BUSY);
volatile bool rxFlag = false;
void onRxDone(void) { rxFlag = true; }

void setup() {
  pinMode(PIN_RFSW_PWR, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(PIN_RFSW_PWR, HIGH);
  pinMode(PIN_RFSW_CTL, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(PIN_RFSW_CTL, HIGH);
  SPI.begin();

  radio.XTAL = true;       /* board treats always-on TCXO as XTAL */
  radio.irqDioNum = 8;     /* Wio-LR2021 routes IRQ to DIO8 */
  /* explicit header; params match the peer node (910.125 MHz, BW 250 kHz,
   * SF9, CR 4/5, sync 0x2B, 10 dBm, preamble 16) */
  int16_t state = radio.begin(910.125, 250.0, 9, 5, 0x2B, 10, 16);
  logf("begin state=%d\r\n", state);
  state = radio.setCRC(2);
  logf("setCRC state=%d\r\n", state);
  radio.setPacketReceivedAction(onRxDone);
}

void runPhase(const char* tag, size_t txLen) {
  uint8_t buf[256];
  for (size_t i = 0; i < txLen; i++) { buf[i] = (uint8_t)i; }

  logf("\r\n%s transmit len=%u\r\n", tag, (unsigned)txLen);
  int16_t state = radio.transmit(buf, txLen);
  logf("  transmit state=%d\r\n", state);

  state = radio.startReceive();
  logf("  startReceive state=%d\r\n", state);
  logf("  listening 75 s - send a packet LARGER than the Tx now\r\n");

  uint32_t start = millis();
  while (millis() - start < 75000UL) {
    if (rxFlag) {
      rxFlag = false;
      size_t len = radio.getPacketLength();
      state = radio.readData(buf, len);
      logf("  *** RX len=%u state=%d at t+%lu ms\r\n",
           (unsigned)len, state, (unsigned long)(millis() - start));
      radio.startReceive();
    }
    delay(50);
  }
  logf("%s window over\r\n", tag);
}

void loop() {
  runPhase("PHASE A (Tx 16 B):", 16);
  runPhase("PHASE B (Tx 200 B):", 200);
}
/* =============================== SKETCH END =============================== */

/* ---- platform boilerplate: run setup()/loop() in a FreeRTOS task ---------- */
extern "C" void consoleUartInit(void);

static void sketch_task(void *arg)
{
    (void)arg;
    setup();
    for (;;) { loop(); }
}

int main(void)
{
    consoleUartInit();
    xTaskCreate(sketch_task, "sketch", 2048, NULL, tskIDLE_PRIORITY + 2, NULL);
    vTaskStartScheduler();
    for (;;) { }
    return 0;
}

/* FreeRTOS static-allocation providers (config has STATIC_ALLOCATION=1). */
extern "C" {
void vApplicationGetIdleTaskMemory(StaticTask_t **tcb, StackType_t **stk, uint32_t *sz)
{
    static StaticTask_t t;
    static StackType_t s[configMINIMAL_STACK_SIZE];
    *tcb = &t; *stk = s; *sz = configMINIMAL_STACK_SIZE;
}
void vApplicationGetTimerTaskMemory(StaticTask_t **tcb, StackType_t **stk, uint32_t *sz)
{
    static StaticTask_t t;
    static StackType_t s[configTIMER_TASK_STACK_DEPTH];
    *tcb = &t; *stk = s; *sz = configTIMER_TASK_STACK_DEPTH;
}
void vApplicationMallocFailedHook(void) { for (;;) {} }
void vApplicationStackOverflowHook(TaskHandle_t x, char *n) { (void)x; (void)n; for (;;) {} }
}

