**Expected behavior**
RX should accept up to the maximum packet length in explicit header mode
regardless of what was last transmitted, as SX126x already does.

I can submit a PR if necessary. The LR11x0 driver has the same implicit-only pattern (without
the ternary) and likely the same latent issue, masked by LoRaWAN-style
traffic (uplinks larger than downlinks) and by the config setters that
incidentally rewrite packet params. I can submit the PR for just the LoRa LR2021 or for both it and the LR11x0 but I haven't actually done any testing with the LR11x0. GFSK also appears to be impacted but haven't done any testing with it and have no fix written for it. 

